	# Pain Points of TurtleBrains:
		☐ 2026-09-19: TurtleBrains Particle System has no editor.
		✔ 2025-10-25: Make SetOrigin() in the tbGraphics::GraphicList public again. @done(20251025 06:55)
			After a quick investigation this was disabled 10 years ago when the GraphicList was first created. Almost
			certainly because we had no RecalculateWidthAndHeight() and had no way of knowing the size to set the origin
			of. RecalculateWidthAndHeight() was added 3 years ago, and could be called during Add or RemoveGraphic.

			The only real gotchya is the Developer will need to call SetOrigin() _again_ if they call Add or Remove
			graphic since the BaseGraphic / graphic list doesn't hold the Anchor with an offset, but just the origin.
		✔ 2025-10-02: GraphicList can't use SetOrigin() which caused pain when trying to position a ButtonEntity. @done(20251025 06:55)
			The full parent tree looked like ButtonEntity is a Entity is a GraphicList ... is a Graphic. But the
			SetOrigin() fails on GraphicList, I assume this was disabled before RecalculateWidthAndHeight() was
			a function. Or perhaps past-Tim didn't want to call a potentially expensive function, or maybe another
			reason I lost track of...
		✘ 2025-10-23: tbGraphics::Camera doesn't have SetPosition(float, float) only Vector2 @cancelled(20260920 09:34)
		✘ 2025-10-09: TurtleBrains Color doesn't have a way to SetAlpha or SetRed etc. @cancelled(20260920 09:34)
			This seems a little odd that it requires setting ALL channels ALL the time.
		✔ 2025-10-01: @hp2 @value5 SetRotation() and GetRotation() on Entity/Sprite/Graphics etc don't use tbMath::Angle @done(20251025 08:31)
			This should begin using the tbMath::Angle since that doesn't care whether developer wants to work in degrees
			or radians for a given function, it simply works.

			It seems likely impossible, but it would be very nice to have this unit tested to spin clockwise. Perhaps the
			unit test could send it to a RenderTarget and compare with a known png/image for likeness?

			Changing GetRotation() would be an @api-break for TurtleBrains and I don't want to deal with the fallout
			of project failing, especially since nightly builds on Windows isn't even setup. SetRotation() now has
			a Angle overload, and there is a "helper function" GetAngle() that can be used in the meantime.

		☐ 2025-10-14: TurtleBrains::Core::Diagnostics::CommandManager has no public "LogToConsole" api.
			This is a huge oversight and for now I've just extern'd the implementation details as a work-around.

			Currently the only available way to do it is implementation::CommandLog which takes a String or a
			printf style const char*/... Ideally this would step away from the printf requirements, it is a bit
			messier, especially when mixed with LogStream already existing... Also a log stream might be able
			to dump to both DeveloperConsole and debug_log.txt at the same time.

			Pro for the stream version is any operator<< overloading just works in all the places.

			tb_debug_log(LogConsole() << "this goes to dev console AND debug_log.txt");
			tbCore::Diagnostics::DeveloperConsole() << "blah blah";

		✔ 2025-10-14: TurtleBrains::Core::Diagnostics::Commands have no built-in 'help' despite messaging. @done(20251025 16:01)
			I was trying to figure out why `give` wasn't working as it did not display with `help` but finally
			figured out that help is not actually displaying the possible commands like I thought it was. That
			must have been done in the Who Let the Dog Out LudumDare code rather than/then inside TurtleBrains.

			2025-10-25: Okay, so I think what happened was a few "BasicCommands" got lost or misplaced when
			bringing the Console / CommandSystem into TurtleBrains. One of those commands was `help` and that
			would explain why there is no... help displayed. Another basic command was `exit` which quit the
			game.


		✔ 2026-01-21: ImGui Editor doesn't accepet the : ; ' " characters @done(20260415 05:37)
			✔ Also doesn't accept any SHIFT numbers !#$ becomes 134 @done(20260415 05:37)
			✔ May want to check for more potential missing spots? @done(20260415 05:37)
		☐ 2025-10-06: Adding a GetClosestMatchingString() string utility would be useful for some error messages.
			I was attempting to ensure all UNLOCK_KEY's added to the TechTree csv file existed in some form to
			prevent issues from typos. It would be neat to also have the messaging suggest "THIS_KEY" was a
			close match.

			This would probably fit in StringUtilities:: with a vector<string> and iterator begin/end option.
